howtoplay.button2= How to Type the Section Sign?
    eer:how_par_pc_header=Computer
    eer:how_par_text2.0= §lTo type the section sign on a computer, you will need a numeric keypad:
    eer:how_par_text2.1=§l1.§r Turn on §lNum Lock§r or §lNL.
    eer:how_par_text2.2=§l2.§r Hold the §lAlt§r key.
    eer:how_par_text2.3=§l3.§r Type §l0167§r on the numeric keypad on the right.
    eer:how_par_text2.4=§l4.§r Release the §lAlt§r key.
    eer:how_par_text2.5=§l5.§r Now you have the sign you need§r.

    eer:how_par_text2.6= Or just copy the symbol: §7Press the line below: Ctrl+A -> Ctrl+C [copy]. Then Ctrl+V [paste].
    eer:how_par_text2.6.1=§
    
    eer:how_par_phone_header=Phone
    eer:how_par_text3.0= §lTo type the section sign on a phone, try these options:§r
    eer:how_par_text3.1= Find the keyboard button that switches to symbols, then look for the  sign.
    eer:how_par_text3.2= If it is not there, try holding symbols like §l'S'§r, §l'&'§r, or §l'%'§r.
    eer:how_par_text3.3= If that still does not work, copy the symbol: §7(if your keyboard allows it).
